Web source  : web/src/features/admin/pages/AuditLogPage.tsx
Output      : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/AuditLogPage/ (namespace TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.Admin)
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked. WinUI/maui-windows workload present.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection, unit-tested
  headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable
  state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7 ApiLogsPage / SchemaDriftPage do. The
  generated prompt's idealized "AuditLogPage.xaml + AuditLogPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Admin" is mapped
  onto these real conventions; the surface registers with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("AuditLog", already in
  RouteTable.cs -> /admin/audit-log) via ShellWindow.xaml.cs.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the four manifest data sources are useAuditLog (GET /admin/audit-log{qs}),
  useAuditCategories (GET /admin/audit-log/categories), useAuditActions (GET /admin/audit-log/actions) and
  useAuditChainVerify (GET /admin/audit-log/verify?limit=). The view-model reads through an injected IAuditLogFeed; the
  default EmptyAuditLogFeed resolves the empty state (the ApiLogsPage/SchemaDriftPage host-injection precedent), and the
  generated-client-backed AuditLogClientFeed (AuditLogPage.Source.cs) binds to the generated OpenAPI contract client
  operations get_api_v1_admin_audit_log[/categories|/actions|/verify], asserted in tests. No HTTP touches the view. A
  non-success list response surfaces as ApiException; the view-model maps StatusCode==503 to the distinct
  subsystem-unavailable banner (web `subsystemMissing`) and every other failure to the generic InfoBar+Retry. The
  category/action facet reads are best-effort (a failed facet leaves the dropdown at "All …", never breaks the page),
  matching the always-enabled web hooks; the chain-verify read is a manual, independent sub-state (web handleVerify).
- The web page renders the four list data states inside the PageContainer body (PageContainer is passed only `query=`),
  so the native port reproduces them as visible Fluent regions per ADR-006: loading -> ProgressRing + caption;
  error -> TsQueryError (InfoBar-equivalent) + Retry; 503 subsystem-missing -> TsAlertBanner(Warning) notConfigured
  above the panels; empty -> TsEmptyState (History glyph); success -> the expandable audit rows. The three web
  GlassPanels (hash-chain integrity, filters, entries) are reproduced as TsGlassPanel/Mica regions, always visible.
  Never a blank region.
- The audit table is composed from shared primitives (the web DataTable's rich cells — Badge, CopyButton, expandable
  detail — are not expressible by the text-only TsDataTable, so the row grid is built from TsBadge / TsCopyButton /
  TsButton exactly as the sibling ApiLogsPage row composes its Expander rows). Each row carries the timestamp +
  relative time, actor, category badge, action, entity (+#id), detail snippet, trace chip (+copy), success badge and a
  Details/Hide toggle; the expanded detail carries IP, user-agent, trace id (+copy), before/after JSON snapshots and the
  row hash (+copy). Filters: since/until (datetime text inputs committed on Enter/blur, normalised to ISO-8601 UTC in
  the client feed exactly as web `new Date(v).toISOString()`), category/action (Select facets), actor/entity-type (text
  inputs), rows-per-page (50/100/250/500, web LIMIT_OPTIONS), plus Reset + Search. Offset pagination (Previous/Next,
  "Showing {from}–{to}") mirrors the web setOffset math; the page resets to offset 0 on any filter change.
- SI units N/A (no unit-bearing fields on this admin surface — ledger rows + a SHA-256 row-hash chain only). Counts
  format through the shared NumberFormatting port (web {{count}}) and timestamps through DateTimeFormatting (web
  formatDateTime / formatRelative) at the display boundary.
- All 50 i18n keys resolve through the ILocalizer facade with the verbatim web key names. The 49 admin.auditLog.* keys
  were added to Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw as translation.admin.auditLog.* (admin.subsystem.unavailableTitle
  already present, shared with the other admin pages). The ar/he catalogs carry the English default until translated;
  the app falls back to the English default via ILocalizer regardless. The two input-hint keys (actorPlaceholder,
  entityTypePlaceholder) carry `// parity:allow` markers (web i18n key names, not stub placeholders).
- W1 materialization: the generated C# client (apps/windows/Generated, gitignored per .gitignore apps/**/generated/)
  was absent from the worktree, so the whole solution failed to build at baseline (CS0234: TeslaSync.Windows.* missing).
  Regenerated it via `npx tsx@4.22.4 apps/tools/codegen/gen-clients.ts` (wrote Generated/Api/*.cs) and scaffolded the
  gitignored Generated/Generated.csproj (modelled on apps/tools/codegen/verify/csharp/Verify.csproj: net10.0, Nullable,
  in-box System.Text.Json, compiles Api/*.cs) that TeslaSync.App.Core references. Both are gitignored build artifacts,
  not committed. Baseline then went green (0 errors).

